   "issue": "The theorem docstring says only that `g` is constant along the fibres of `\u03c1` in `U \u2229 S`. The hypothesis `hg\u03c1 : \u2200 x \u2208 U \u2229 S, \u03c1 x \u2208 S \u2227 g (\u03c1 x) = g x` also requires `\u03c1` to map `U \u2229 S` into `S`. Since `g` is defined on all of `M`, this extra condition is not implied, so the docstring describes the result as more general than it is.",
